  "id": "Compound::DB00611 - Gene::4988",
  "verbalization": "Butorphanol's relationship with Oprm1 is supported by its classification as both a competitive opioid antagonist and a partial opioid agonist, with Pentazocine serving as a common bridge between these categories. This dual classification suggests that Butorphanol may interact with Oprm1 through mechanisms that involve competitive binding and partial activation of the receptor, potentially leading to complex signaling outcomes. The shared pathway to Oprm1, through the Opioid and Organonitrogen Compound classes, indicates a common biological context in which Butorphanol and Pentazocine exert their effects. The evidence suggests that Butorphanol may modulate Oprm1 activity through a mechanism that involves receptor binding and possibly downstream signaling, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering both agonist and antagonist properties in understanding the therapeutic effects of Butorphanol on opioid receptors.",
